# Volt customisation kits

The Volt has 15 new choices in each of its hood, rear aero, rims and body-kit categories, plus Original. The parts use the existing independent Garage preview, ownership, equip and reset flow. The selected IDs are stored in vehicle appearances and used by races and ghosts; they do not change handling. Original rims are kept in replaceable wheel frames so tires and steering remain independent.

The Electric server catalogue, ownership checks and coin prices include all 60 options. Account purchases and sync require the matching backend code to be deployed; this work did not deploy it. The new option names and descriptions currently fall back to English in other languages; translations and a refreshed complete localisation catalogue remain outstanding.

The 120 full/simple modular kit scenes and four Volt base scenes were rebuilt. Actual Garage previews are shown in [hood](evidence/volt-kits-2026-11-01/hood_volt_triple.png), [rear aero](evidence/volt-kits-2026-11-01/aero_volt_gt.png), [rims](evidence/volt-kits-2026-11-01/rims_volt_mesh.png), [body](evidence/volt-kits-2026-11-01/body_volt_race.png), and the [parts list](evidence/volt-kits-2026-11-01/garage-rims.png).

The native option test passed 578 checks, including all choices, both qualities, distinct geometry and original restoration. The exhaustive prepared-asset comparison passed 1,788 checks; the actual Compatibility Garage, local save/reload, purchase-cancel, race and ghost test passed 54. Tire clearance passed 79; retained kart geometry passed 822. Backend Volt and other kit tests passed 165, and retained economy/appearance tests passed 106 with one skipped and PostgreSQL cases excluded. An existing economy test's stale kart count and its vehicle filter were updated. Godot import completed with an unavailable Android build-tools warning; no device test or live-account transaction was performed.
